    "intro": {
      "id": "intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The screenshot judge is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "V-judge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", a vision model that rates each page's state screenshots against taste rules such as hierarchy, grouping and polish. Its area holds 32 rules: the 26 rules mapped to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "V-judge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and 6 process rules that need a person or a model. The rules are in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "design-score/rules/judge.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "design-score/rules/judge.json"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and the judge is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "runJudge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "scripts/design-score/judge.ts",
              "symbol": "runJudge"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "planned": {
      "id": "planned",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "title": "Opt-in",
        "tone": "info"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "V-judge runs only with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "bun run design:score --judge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", because each screenshot costs a model call. Without the flag every page marks it n/a."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "h-how": {
      "id": "h-how",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "How It Works"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "how-lead": {
      "id": "how-lead",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The judge reads the state screenshots the run already took, so it never picks an easy screen. Each screenshot goes through these steps."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "how1": {
      "id": "how1",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The run saves the state screenshot of each page, theme and viewport as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "shots/<page>__<theme>__<viewport>.png",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "how2": {
      "id": "how2",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The cheap model, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "claude-haiku-5-5",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", answers pass, fail, unsure or n/a for each of the 16 still rules. Each answer has a short reason, and each fail or unsure has a box."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "how3": {
      "id": "how3",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "On any fail or unsure, the strong model, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "claude-opus-5-5",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", rates the same screenshot again. Its answers are final."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "how4": {
      "id": "how4",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A strong fail is a fail finding, and a strong unsure is a warn finding for Ford. A rule that the cheap model flagged and the strong model passed goes to the review list, and it never counts."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "how5": {
      "id": "how5",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every reply is cached under the hash of its request: the screenshot bytes, the model and the prompt. A rerun over the same pixels makes no call."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "how-after": {
      "id": "how-after",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A judge finding has the same shape as every other finding, with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "check: \"V-judge\"",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It cites one rule id in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "rules",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", the reason in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "measured",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and the rule text in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "expected",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The run writes the call count, the cache hits, the token usage, the cost and the review list to the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "judge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " field of "
        },
        {
          "insert": "scorecard.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "h-cal": {
      "id": "h-cal",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Calibration"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "cal-lead": {
      "id": "cal-lead",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The judge must agree with known answers before its findings count. Three label sets give those answers. Issue 20 is the first set, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "calibrate",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "scripts/design-score/judge-calibrate.ts",
              "symbol": "calibrate"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " scores the judge on it."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "cal1": {
      "id": "cal1",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Interfaces Magazine issue 20",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "cal1a",
        "cal1b",
        "cal1c"
      ]
    },
    "cal1a": {
      "id": "cal1a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Issue 20, \"Can you tell the difference?\", has 27 A/B questions, each with its answer and the reason."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "cal1b": {
      "id": "cal1b",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "10 questions compare still frames, and 14 compare motion. The other 3 are knowledge questions for a text-only judge."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "cal1c": {
      "id": "cal1c",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The posters and clips, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "demo-02.png",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "demo-27.mp4",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", are not in git, because their licence does not allow a copy. Pass their folder with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--media",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "cal2": {
      "id": "cal2",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Pairs Ford labels",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "cal2a",
        "cal2b"
      ]
    },
    "cal2a": {
      "id": "cal2a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Ford labels 30 to 50 before and after pairs from real runs as better, same or worse."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "cal2b": {
      "id": "cal2b",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The judge is tuned to Ford's taste, because professional designers often disagree with each other."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "cal3": {
      "id": "cal3",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Held-out pairs",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "cal3a"
      ]
    },
    "cal3a": {
      "id": "cal3a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Labelled pairs from issues 09, 16 and 19, with the labels masked, test the judge on data it was not tuned on."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "h-bar": {
      "id": "h-bar",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Pass Bar and Cost Cap"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "bar-lead": {
      "id": "bar-lead",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "These limits are proposals, and Ford sets the final numbers before the first judge run."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "bar1": {
      "id": "bar1",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Pass bar",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "bar1a",
        "bar1b"
      ]
    },
    "bar1a": {
      "id": "bar1a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The judge counts in a score only while it agrees with Ford on 80% or more of the labelled pairs."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "bar1b": {
      "id": "bar1b",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Below that bar, its findings are advisory and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "V-judge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " stays n/a. A finding fails a page only on a confident no from the strong model."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "bar2": {
      "id": "bar2",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Cost cap",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "bar2a",
        "bar2b"
      ]
    },
    "bar2a": {
      "id": "bar2a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Only a fail or unsure from the cheap model goes to the strong model. Cached replies cost nothing."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "bar2b": {
      "id": "bar2b",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A run stops at 100 uncached calls by default. At the cap the judge reports the screenshots it did not judge."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "bar-open": {
      "id": "bar-open",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "title": "Open decision",
        "tone": "info"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Ford sets the pass bar. Until then, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--judge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " counts V-judge in the score, and a run without it leaves V-judge n/a."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "h-built": {
      "id": "h-built",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "What Is Built"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "built-lead": {
      "id": "built-lead",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The judge, its fixture pair and the calibration are built. Ford's own labels and the held-out issues are not."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "built1": {
      "id": "built1",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The judge",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "built1a"
      ]
    },
    "built1a": {
      "id": "built1a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "runJudge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "scripts/design-score/judge.ts",
              "symbol": "runJudge"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rates the state screenshots after every other check. The run writes its summary to the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "judge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " field of "
        },
        {
          "insert": "scorecard.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "built2": {
      "id": "built2",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The fixture pair",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "built2a"
      ]
    },
    "built2a": {
      "id": "built2a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "design-score/fixtures/V-judge/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " holds a status list that shows status by color alone, and one that adds a word. The test stubs the model, so it costs nothing, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--fixture V-judge --judge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " runs it with the real model."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "built3": {
      "id": "built3",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
