    },
    "built4a": {
      "id": "built4a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Ford's labelled pairs, the held-out pairs from issues 09, 16 and 19, and frame strips for motion rules in a real run do not exist yet."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "h-why": {
      "id": "h-why",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why This Design"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "why-lead": {
      "id": "why-lead",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Three studies shape the plan."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "why1": {
      "id": "why1",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "MLLM as a UI Judge",
          "attributes": {
            "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.08783"
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "why1a"
      ]
    },
    "why1a": {
      "id": "why1a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Models agreed with people best on factors with concrete visual cues, such as visual hierarchy. That is why each question names one cue."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "why2": {
      "id": "why2",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "DesignPref",
          "attributes": {
            "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.20513"
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "why2a"
      ]
    },
    "why2a": {
      "id": "why2a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "20 professional designers made 12,000 pairwise choices and often disagreed. That is why Ford's labels calibrate the judge."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "why3": {
      "id": "why3",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Trust or Escalate (ICLR 2025)",
          "attributes": {
            "link": "https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2025/file/08dabd5345b37fffcbe335bd578b15a0-Paper-Conference.pdf"
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        "why3a"
      ]
    },
    "why3a": {
      "id": "why3a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A small labelled set decides when to trust a judge and when to ask a person. That is why unsure answers go to Ford."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "h-rules": {
      "id": "h-rules",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Rules"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "rules-lead": {
      "id": "rules-lead",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "26 rules map to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "V-judge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in five groups, and each row gives the yes or no question the judge asks. A yes passes. The still judge asks 16 of them, and the Choices section names the 10 it skips."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "h-g1": {
      "id": "h-g1",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Layout and Hierarchy"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "t-g1": {
      "id": "t-g1",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Rule",
          "Title",
          "Question"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "layout-importance-order",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Importance order",
            "Does the most important content sit top and leading, with metadata and actions after it?"
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "layout-separators-last",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Separators last",
            "Does each separator sit where space alone cannot show the structure?"
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "layout-static-not-control-shaped",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Static is not control-shaped",
            "Does each static badge look different from the buttons beside it?"
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "layout-content-bleeds-controls-float",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Content bleeds, controls stay inside",
            "Do controls and text stay inside the layout margins?"
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "layout-rtl-mirror",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "RTL mirror",
            "Under dir=rtl, does the layout mirror cleanly? Only for apps that support RTL."
          ],
          [
